REMARKS:
280900Z POSITION NEAR 16.7N 81.8E.
28OCT26. TROPICAL CYCLONE 02B (ARNAB), LOCATED APPROXIMATELY 527
NM SOUTHWEST OF KOLKATA, INDIA, HAS TRACKED NORTHEASTWARD AT 03
KNOTS OVER THE PAST SIX HOURS. AS TROPICAL CYCLONE (TC) 02B 
APPROACHED LAND THIS MORNING, IT RAPIDLY DECLERATED, AND TURNING 
SOUTHWESTWARD, DUE TO THE COMBINED EFFECTS OF LAND INTERACTION 
AND BINARY INTERACTION WITH INVEST 90B TO THE EAST. THE SYSTEM 
SKIRTED THE COAST OF THE GODAVARI RIVER DELTA, REACHING A 
POSITION SOUTHWEST OF NARSAPUR BY 0000Z. SINCE THAT TIME, THE 
SYSTEM HAS SLOWLY DRIFTED NORTHWARD AND IS NOW SITUATED ALONG 
THE COASTLINE, IN THE VICINITY OF NARSAPUR BASED ON ANIMATED 
MULTISPECTRAL SATELLITE IMAGERY (MSI) AND RADAR DATA FROM IMD. 
SURFACE OBS FROM NARSAPUR REPORT LIGHT WINDS, AND MEAN SEA 
LEVEL PRESSURE OF 988MB, WHICH SUPPORTS THE INITIAL INTENSITY 
OF 55 KNOTS WITH MEDIUM CONFIDENCE. NOW THAT INVEST 90B HAS 
MADE LANDFALL AND IS MOVING RAPIDLY NORTHWESTWARD INTO INTERIOR 
INDIA, 02B SHOULD START LIFTING NORTHWARD, MOVING ALONG THE 
WESTERN SIDE OF THE SUBTROPICAL RIDGE (STR) TO THE EAST. 02B 
WILL CONTINUE TO STEADILY WEAKEN OVER THE NEXT 36 HOURS, BEFORE 
DISSIPATING OVER NORTHEASTERN INDIA. THIS IS THE FINAL WARNING ON THIS SYSTEM BY THE JOINT TYPHOON
WRNCEN PEARL HARBOR HI. THE SYSTEM WILL BE CLOSELY MONITORED FOR
SIGNS OF REGENERATION. MINIMUM CENTRAL PRESSURE AT 280600Z IS 988
MB.
